class.description:
Enables the "F6 single-screen debug" workflow for [Activity], [Dialog], and [Toast]. When the entering node is the [member SceneTree.current_scene] and no [Application] has been bound to it (i.e. it was not started via [ActivityManager]), this launcher delegates to [method StandaloneApplication.host] to spawn the host environment, then the node adopts itself and dispatches its lifecycle.

Gate (must ALL hold for [code]try_launch[/code] to take effect):
- no [Application] is bound to the node yet (not the normal ActivityManager-injected flow, nor an already-completed bootstrap);
- the engine is in runtime mode, not editor inspector parsing;
- a [SceneTree] is available;
- [member force_standalone] is [code]true[/code] OR the node is the SceneTree's [code]current_scene[/code].

The launcher operates on the shared C++ [code]IContext[/code] interface, so a single instance serves Activity and Dialog identically.

Set [member force_standalone] to launch the node even when it is not the entry scene (useful for editor-side "Play This" buttons).

Set [member play_transitions] to animate the node's [code]transition_in[/code] during the bootstrap. Default is [code]false[/code] so the UI is visible immediately for debugging.
